        "abstract": "Two diode-pumped Nd/sup 3+/-doped fibre lasers have been developed, operating at 935 nm and 1092 nm. These have been used successfully in the laser cooling of Yb/sup +/ and Sr/sup +/. Linewidths of approximately 100 MHz and approximately 300 MHz have been achieved respectively on the cooling transition of the two ion species.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
